# Per-Dockerfile override (BuildKit convention: <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore
# in the context root takes precedence over the context-root .dockerignore,
# for this Dockerfile's build only). service/.dockerignore stays unchanged
# and still applies to the other 6 Dockerfiles in this context.
#
# Two problems, one file, same root cause:
#
# 1. Build defect: service/.dockerignore only whitelists scripts/, but
#    Dockerfile.counselclear also COPYs requirements-app.txt and app/ --
#    both outside that whitelist, so the build fails at the first COPY
#    (see docs/commercial-surface-manifest.md §4). This file's base
#    whitelist adds both.
# 2. Commercial-surface exposure: scripts/ contains adapters that exist
#    to interface with CtrlRegen (no LICENSE -- all-rights-reserved) and
#    reverse-SynthID (non-commercial Research License). They were never
#    vendored, but they shipped inside this image via the blanket
#    `COPY scripts` (see docs/commercial-surface-manifest.md §0.1, §2.1,
#    §2.3, §3 for the full classification and verification). Nothing in
#    service/app/ imports any of the files denied below -- the product
#    path depends only on image_meta.py/engine_api.py themselves, not on
#    these standalone adapter/CLI/server files (verified by grep before
#    this change; see the commit message).
#
# NOT addressed here: the member-level items in commercial-surface-manifest.md
# §2.3 (specific functions/flags inside image_meta.py, engine_api.py,
# text_detectors.py, rewrite_text.py -- e.g. run_synthid_score,
# remove_pixel, MarkLLMTextDetector). Those modules are shared product
# code and stay; removing individual members is a code change, not a
# build-context change, and is deliberately out of scope for this pass.

*
!requirements-app.txt
!app/
!app/**
!scripts/
!scripts/**

# File-level QUARANTINE items (commercial-surface-manifest.md §2.1):
# dedicated adapter/harness CLIs, their pin files, and host bootstrap
# scripts. Nothing in service/app/ imports any of these.
scripts/clean_ctrlregen.py
scripts/score_synthid.py
scripts/synthid_score_server.py
scripts/markdiffusion_harness.py
scripts/detect_text_watermark.py
scripts/bench_synthid_text.py
scripts/requirements-ctrlregen.txt
scripts/requirements-synthid-scorer.txt
scripts/requirements-markllm.txt
scripts/requirements-markdiffusion.txt
scripts/setup_ctrlregen.sh
scripts/setup_ctrlregen.ps1
scripts/setup_synthid.sh
scripts/setup_synthid.ps1
scripts/setup_markllm.sh
scripts/setup_markdiffusion.sh

# Legacy wr-core CLI/server surface (commercial-surface-manifest.md
# §2.3): standalone entry points for the upstream-utility tool, not
# used by the CounselClear app. clean_image.py/inspect_image.py import
# FROM image_meta.py (which stays) -- nothing imports these files
# themselves.
scripts/clean_image.py
scripts/inspect_image.py
scripts/server.py
scripts/ui.html

# Never ship build/runtime junk even though it sits under scripts/ or app/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
